DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("sin(((sin(x))-3))");
$fun_1 = Formula("e^((ln(x)))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("(3, infinity) U {0, 8}");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("(3, infinity) U {0, 8}");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("{0, 8} U (3, infinity) U ((3, infinity) U {0, 8}) U {0, 8}");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("(((1, infinity)) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ((4, 9)))) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ((4, 9))) U ((4, 9))");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("(4, 14) U (4, 9) U (4, 14) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (4, 9))");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

What is the value of [`7*4+7/4`]? [_____]{answer=>29.75,width=>10}
---

What is the value of [`5+1*0.46`]? [_____]{answer=>Formula('5.46'),width=>7}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | 4 < x < 9\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x > 0\}`]
- [`C = \{x | 4 < x < 14\}`]

Compute:
- [`((B) \cap (A)) \cap (A) \cup (A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`C \cup A \cup C \cap A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{0, 8\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x > 2\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`B \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`A \cup B \cup (B \cup A) \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -7, 9, -8 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -3, 4, 3 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-7, 9, -8>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-3, 4, 3>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-3, 4, 3>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-7, 9, -8>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 8, 10, 1 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 6, 5, -2 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<6, 5, -2>") . Compute("<8, 10, 1>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<6, 5, -2>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<6, 5, -2>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<8, 10, 1>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<6, 5, -2>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<8, 10, 1>"))}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f'(1) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>1)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(6) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>6)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(6) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>6)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();